  "lineage": "Village song traditions of Thailand's Central, Northern and Isan regions — repartee genres such as lam klon, phleng choi and so phrae — carried by itinerant singers into the twentieth century and documented by mid-century field collectors, built on free-reed khaen drone-and-ostinato, plucked phin or sueng, hand-drum and ching cymbal timekeeping, and rapid syllabic call-and-response verse improvised over a single mode.",
